{:edb/db-before-t 1933 :edb/db-after-t 1934 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535246 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:24:05.959Z" 13194139535246 true] [17592186096754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339712 13194139535246 true] [17592186096755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186339709 13194139535246 true] [17592186339709 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339710 13194139535246 true] [17592186339709 1089 "q-351049" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339709 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535246 true] [17592186339709 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339709 1113 #uuid "a03fd2b0-369d-5e9a-a0ba-867654d1e366" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339709 1145 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{4}{4x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}-{\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)\\,(x){|}_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}-{\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}x(\\frac{4}{4x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})(\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{4})-{\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}\\frac{4x}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{4}\\cdot 2-{\\int }_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4}(1-\\frac{1}{4x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}-{[x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x+1)]}_{0}^{({e}^{2}-1)/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}-(\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}-(\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339711 13194139535246 true] [17592186339710 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535246 true] [17592186339710 1041 "field-1" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339710 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339711 13194139535246 true] [17592186339710 1110 #uuid "d7c3c7f6-b15a-5392-928f-0dd50b0aa767" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339711 1034 "\\frac{e^2+1}{4}" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535246 true] [17592186339711 1111 #uuid "5d9dd781-040d-5b5b-ae86-becc6878db7b" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339712 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339713 13194139535246 true] [17592186339712 1089 "q-78964" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339712 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535246 true] [17592186339712 1100 "Calculate $\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339712 1113 #uuid "22c481da-5f59-5a94-b0f0-466987b6a096" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339712 1145 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5} \\\\ {v}^{′}=25{x}^{4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(5x)\\cdot (5{x}^{5})-\\int \\frac{5{x}^{5}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{log}_{5}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot {x}^{5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{5}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.$" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339714 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339715 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339716 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339717 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339718 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1041 "selection" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339715 13194139535246 true] [17592186339713 1110 #uuid "9c9749b9-7526-5c01-9741-db41e8608590" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339714 1034 "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)+1)+C" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535246 true] [17592186339714 1111 #uuid "94797d45-9919-5857-a21b-be221721a82e" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339715 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-1)+C" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535246 true] [17592186339715 1111 #uuid "8fea396c-1162-5caa-9480-0fdcd3de192f" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339716 1034 "\\frac{25{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-1)+C" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535246 true] [17592186339716 1111 #uuid "b4532591-3b15-578a-aac5-2d4e61b6f7e6" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339717 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-1)+C" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535246 true] [17592186339717 1111 #uuid "1157d581-7a21-56ea-8ad1-63187734e110" 13194139535246 true] [17592186339718 1034 "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-1)+C" 131